// Populate [CR#701.36a]: "choose a creature token you control, then create a
// token that's a copy of that creature token." If you control no creature
// tokens, populate does nothing ([CR#701.36b]) — the `ChooseOne` binder over an
// empty candidate set makes no choice, so the inner `Create` never runs (a copy
// of nothing creates nothing, the same fizzle `token_copy_nonexistent_source`
// exercises). A composite keyword action ([CR#701.36]): it names no new engine
// primitive, decomposing into the copy grammar's `Create(1, Copy(...))` under a
// `With(ChooseOne(...))` binder — the "choose a … you control" shape.
//
// The filter is `Kind(Token) ∧ Creature ∧ you control` — a creature token you
// control ([CR#701.36a]). `Kind(Token)` is `Predicate::Kind(ObjectKind::Token)`.
// A `With` one-binder (`ChooseOne`) binds its pick as `Reference::That` (the
// engine's `resolve/effect.rs` sets only `anaphora.that`, never `it`, for a
// `With`; `It` would fizzle unbound here). The copy source therefore reads
// `Object(That(Token))`: the `That` SORT must match what the Idris re-emit gate
// derives for this filter — `filterSort` pins `Kind(Token)` to the `Token` sort
// on the battlefield (`Core.idr`), and `compat` accepts `That(Token)` but NOT
// `That(Creature)` against it (the sort is verified only by Idris; the engine
// ignores it at runtime). An `OneShotEffect`-kind macro, so `Populate` stands as
// the effect body of any shell (a spell, an ETB, an activated ability), plus
// `KeywordAction` so it's recognized as one ([CR#701]).
(
    name: "Populate",
    template: "populate",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    body: With(
        binder: ChooseOne(filter: And([
            Kind(Token),
            Type("Creature"),
            ControlledBy(Ref(You)),
        ])),
        body: Create(1, Copy(source: Object(That(Token)), exceptions: [])),
    ),
)
